Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:16:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 165/165] PC5: a decoded video picture's buffer reports its
 whole length, all its planes (Wine patch 1037)

A Media Foundation buffer holding a Direct3D 11 texture answered DXVK's DepthPitch as its length, which for NV12 is the luma plane only (2088960 of a 1920x1088 picture's 3133440). Unreal Engine 5's Electra H.264 decoder checks the length against Pitch x Height x 3 / 2, stopped its decoder thread at the first picture, and Rec Rewind stayed on its loading screen. The length is now the whole picture at the mapped pitch.
---
 ...buffer-s-length-is-the-whole-picture.patch | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1037-mfplat-a-direct3d-11-surface-buffer-s-length-is-the-whole-picture.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1037-mfplat-a-direct3d-11-surface-buffer-s-length-is-the-whole-picture.patch b/wine/patches/1037-mfplat-a-direct3d-11-surface-buffer-s-length-is-the-whole-picture.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f8e57c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1037-mfplat-a-direct3d-11-surface-buffer-s-length-is-the-whole-picture.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] mfplat: A Direct3D 11 surface buffer's length is the whole
+ picture.
+
+Lock2DSize on a buffer holding a Direct3D 11 texture answered the
+mapped texture's DepthPitch as the buffer's length. For a planar
+format, DXVK's DepthPitch is the first plane: a 1920x1088 NV12 picture
+gave 2088960, its luma, where the buffer holds 3133440 with its chroma.
+Unreal Engine 5's Electra H.264 decoder checks that the length is at
+least Pitch x DecodedHeight x 3 / 2, so its decoder thread stopped on
+the first picture and Rec Rewind stayed on its loading screen.
+
+The length is now the whole picture at the mapped pitch: the buffer's
+plane size scaled from its own stride to RowPitch, or DepthPitch if
+that is more, as the copy into the buffer already takes both planes.
+---
+ dlls/mfplat/buffer.c | 10 +++++++++-
+ 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/dlls/mfplat/buffer.c b/dlls/mfplat/buffer.c
+index 6d59245..e1c4f8d 100644
+--- a/dlls/mfplat/buffer.c
++++ b/dlls/mfplat/buffer.c
+@@ -1117,7 +1117,15 @@ static HRESULT dxgi_surface_buffer_lock(struct buffer *buffer, MF2DBuffer_LockFl
+         if (buffer_start)
+             *buffer_start = *scanline0;
+         if (buffer_length)
+-            *buffer_length = buffer->dxgi_surface.map_desc.DepthPitch;
++        {
++            /* The whole picture, all its planes at the mapped pitch, as Windows has it: a
++             * planar format's DepthPitch may be its first plane only (DXVK's NV12 is RowPitch x
++             * Height), and a decoder that checks the length against Pitch x Height x 3 / 2
++             * stops (Unreal Engine 5's Electra H.264 decoder). */
++            UINT64 length = buffer->_2d.width ? (UINT64)buffer->_2d.plane_size *
++                    buffer->dxgi_surface.map_desc.RowPitch / buffer->_2d.width : 0;
++            *buffer_length = max(buffer->dxgi_surface.map_desc.DepthPitch, (DWORD)min(length, MAXDWORD));
++        }
+     }
+ 
+     return hr;
